<section class="hero"><div class="wrap hero-content"><div><p class="eyebrow">A living portfolio / 2025</p><h1 class="display">Power, in<br>its place.</h1><p class="hero-copy">A closer look at solar projects shaped by their surroundings — and the people who make them work.</p><a class="text-link" href="#work"><span class="circle-arrow">↓</span> Start exploring</a></div><div class="hero-index"><span>Places in focus</span><strong>01 — 03</strong></div></div></section>
<section id="approach" class="section"><div class="wrap premise"><div><p class="section-marker mono">01 / The premise</p><div class="rule"></div></div><div><h2 class="display">Good energy<br>belongs <em>somewhere.</em></h2><div class="two-copy"><p>Every site has its own geometry: a roofline to follow, a horizon to respect, a demand curve to meet. The work starts by listening to the place.</p><p>These illustrative studies make that work visible. Not just the panel count, but the careful decisions that turn available sunlight into useful power.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section id="work" class="section work"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="section-kicker mono">02 / Selected work</p><h2 class="section-title display">Three places.<br><em>One bright idea.</em></h2></div><p class="section-intro">An illustrative portfolio across landscapes, rooftops and shared spaces. Select a typology to explore.</p></div><div class="filters" aria-label="Filter projects"><button class="filter-btn" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All work</button><button class="filter-btn" data-filter="Ground mount" aria-pressed="false">Ground mount</button><button class="filter-btn" data-filter="Rooftop" aria-pressed="false">Rooftop</button><button class="filter-btn" data-filter="Canopy + storage" aria-pressed="false">Canopy + storage</button></div><div class="project-grid"><article class="project-card" data-type="Ground mount"><div class="project-photo"><span class="case-label">01 / Case study</span><h3 class="project-name display">Mesa / 01</h3></div><div class="project-info"><div class="project-type-line"><span>High desert · Utility scale</span><span>Ground mount</span></div><div class="project-metric"><span class="project-size display">18.4 MWp</span><span class="metric-caption">Illustrative output · 31.2 GWh / yr</span></div></div></article><article class="project-card" data-type="Rooftop"><div class="project-photo"><span class="case-label">02 / Case study</span><h3 class="project-name display">Stillwater Works</h3></div><div class="project-info"><div class="project-type-line"><span>River district · Industrial</span><span>Rooftop</span></div><div class="project-metric"><span class="project-size display">2.8 MWp</span><span class="metric-caption">Illustrative output · 4.6 GWh / yr</span></div></div></article><article class="project-card" data-type="Canopy + storage"><div class="project-photo"><span class="case-label">03 / Case study</span><h3 class="project-name display">Northline Commons</h3></div><div class="project-info"><div class="project-type-line"><span>Inland valley · Community</span><span>Canopy + storage</span></div><div class="project-metric"><span class="project-size display">640 kWp</span><span class="metric-caption">Illustrative storage · 1.2 MWh</span></div></div></article></div><p class="sample-note mono">Project names, system sizes and all performance figures are illustrative samples.</p></div></section>
<section class="section sun-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="sun-copy"><div><p class="section-marker mono">03 / Built around the brief</p><h2 class="display">Different ground.<br>Different answers.</h2></div><p>The most effective system is rarely a copy of the last one. We look for the fit between site, use and ambition — then make the infrastructure feel like it belongs.</p></div><div id="method" class="steps"><article class="step"><span class="label">01 — Method</span><h3 class="display">Read the site</h3><p>Sun path, structural limits and the shape of the land set the first coordinates.</p></article><article class="step"><span class="label">02 — Method</span><h3 class="display">Shape the system</h3><p>Generation, storage and connection are balanced against the real use case.</p></article><article class="step"><span class="label">03 — Method</span><h3 class="display">Make it last</h3><p>Service access, monitoring and thoughtful detailing matter long after commissioning.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="impact" class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="impact-head"><div><p class="section-marker mono">04 / In perspective</p><h2 class="section-title display">The work,<br>in <em>numbers.</em></h2></div><p>A useful way to see the scale of a system is to consider the energy it can make and the role it can play on-site.</p></div><div class="metrics"><article class="metric"><div><span class="metric-value display">21.8</span> <span class="metric-unit">MWp</span></div><p class="metric-caption-light">Illustrative combined capacity</p></article><article class="metric"><div><span class="metric-value display">37.0</span> <span class="metric-unit">GWh</span></div><p class="metric-caption-light">Illustrative annual generation</p></article><article class="metric"><div><span class="metric-value display">1.2</span> <span class="metric-unit">MWh</span></div><p class="metric-caption-light">Illustrative storage capacity</p></article><article class="metric"><div><span class="metric-value display">03</span> <span class="metric-unit">sites</span></div><p class="metric-caption-light">Illustrative project studies</p></article></div><p class="impact-note">All figures on this page are illustrative samples, not measured project results.</p></div></section>
<section class="cta"><div class="wrap cta-inner"><div><p class="section-kicker mono">05 / The next site is yours</p><h2 class="display">Start with<br>the place.</h2></div><div><p>Every project begins with a different question. Explore the studies above, or return to the top and take another look.</p><a class="cta-button" href="#work">Back to selected work ↗</a></div></div></section>
